===[ ML: RoadMap ]==============================================================
1|> Math Foundations for ML
    * Goal: Build a strong mathematical foundation for understanding ML
            algorithms.
    > Topics:
      - Linear Algebra                                                  | Done
      - Calculus
        . derivatives                                                   | Done
        . partial derivatives                                           | Done
        . Integrals                                                     | ...
      - Probability & Statistics:
        . Descriptive statistics                                        | Done
        . Inferential Statistics                                        | ...

2|> Machine Learning Theory
    * Goal: Understand the theoretical principles behind machine learning models
    > Topics:
      - supervised & unsupervised learning                              | Done
      - Linear Regression                                               | Done
      - Multiple Linear Regression                                      | Done
      - Plynomial Regression                                            | Done 
      - Regression VS Classification                                    | Done
      - Logistic Regression                                             | Done
      - Overfitting & Underfitting                                      | Done

3|> ML - Fundamentals (tools and workflow)
    * Goal: Understand basic AI/ML workflow and core tools.
    > Topics:
      - NumPy & Pandas (data preprocessing/handling) 
        . NumPy                                                         | Done
        . Pandas                                                        | Done
      - Matplotlib/Seaborn (data visualization)                       
        . Matplotlib                                                    | Done 
        . Seaborn                                                       | Done 
      - Scikit-learn (basic ML models)                                  | Done 
    > Resources:
      - NumPy Quickstart
        |=> 'https://numpy.org/doc/stable/user/quickstart.html'
      - Kaggle Pandas & NumPy Courses
        |=> 'https://www.kaggle.com/learn'
      - Scikit-learn tutorials
        |=> 'https://scikit-learn.org/stable/tutorial/index.html'

4|> Practical Machine Learning
    * Goal: Learn the ML process — preprocessing, training, evaluation.
    > Topics:
      - Supervised learning (classification, regression)                | Done
      - Model evaluation (confusion matrix, metrics)                    | Done 
    > Mini-Projects:
      - Predict housing prices (regression)                             | Done
      - Classify iris or MNIST digits                                   | Done
    > Resources:
      - Hands-On ML with Scikit-Learn (GitHub repo)
        |=> "https://github.com/ageron/handson-ml2"
      - ML Crash Course by Google
        |=> "https://developers.google.com/machine-learning/crash-course"

5|> Deep Learning Foundations
    * Goal: Build neural networks and understand how deep models work.
    > Topics:
      - Neural networks, backpropagation                                |
      - PyTorch or TensorFlow basics                                    |
    > Resources:
      - Deep Learning with PyTorch: A 60 Minute Blitz
        |=> "https://pytorch.org/tutorials/beginner/deep_learning_60min_blitz.html"
      - TensorFlow Beginner Tutorial
        |=> 'https://www.tensorflow.org/tutorials/quickstart/beginner'
      - Fast.ai course (Highly practical)
        |=> 'https://course.fast.ai/' 

6|> Specialization: Computer Vision & YOLO
    * Goal: Apply AI to real-world images using YOLO.
    > Topics:
      - CNNs, image preprocessing                                       |
      - YOLOv5 or YOLOv8 for object detection                           |
    > Resources:
      - YOLOv5 Docs & Tutorials
        |=> 'https://docs.ultralytics.com/'
      - FreeCodeCamp Computer Vision Course
      - Roboflow: Annotate + Train YOLO
        |=> 'https://blog.roboflow.com/how-to-train-yolov5-on-a-custom-dataset/' 

7|> Build Projects
    * Goal: Apply everything you learned.
    > Ideas:
      - Object detection with YOLO on custom images                     |
      - Face mask detection                                             |
      - Real-time webcam object detection                               |
    > Resources:
      - Kaggle
        |=> 'https://www.kaggle.com/'
      - Awesome Deep Learning Projects on GitHub
        |=> 'https://github.com/aymericdamien/TensorFlow-Examples'

# TIP:==========================================================================
# - Focus on one tool per week.                                                |
# - Work on mini-projects — they accelerate understanding.                     |
# - Don't get stuck on theory — code > theory early on.                        |
# ==============================================================================

